{"answer":"Let S_n=1+3+5+\\cdots+(2n-1). For n=1, S_1=1=1^2. If S_k=k^2, then S_{k+1}=S_k+(2(k+1)-1)=k^2+2k+1=(k+1)^2. Thus, by induction, S_n=n^2 for every positive integer n.","approaches":[{"description":"Finite induction using the recurrence obtained by appending the next odd number.","id":"induction-proof","outcome":"candidate","reason":"It proves the stated identity for the base case and preserves it from k to k+1."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"question_premise","basis_reference":"The question asks for the identity for every positive integer n.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"identity-target","kind":"definition","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"For positive integer n, write S_n=1+3+5+\\cdots+(2n-1).","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by the base case and inductive step in steps base-case, inductive-step, and induction-conclusion.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["identity-target"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"odd-sum-square","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"For every positive integer n, S_n=n^2.","step_ids":["base-case","inductive-step","induction-conclusion"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":["identity-target"],"id":"base-case","justification":"S_1=1, and 1=1^2.","statement":"The identity holds when n=1."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["identity-target"],"id":"inductive-step","justification":"Appending the next term gives S_{k+1}=S_k+(2(k+1)-1). Substituting S_k=k^2 yields k^2+2k+1=(k+1)^2.","statement":"For every positive integer k, if S_k=k^2, then S_{k+1}=(k+1)^2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["base-case","inductive-step"],"id":"induction-conclusion","justification":"The base case establishes the assertion at 1, and the inductive step establishes it at each successor once it holds at the preceding positive integer.","statement":"Therefore S_n=n^2 for every positive integer n."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}

